     *   chain has no CCTPx deployment; `INPUT_INVALID_CHAIN` (`FATAL`) when it
     *   has no CCTP domain; `INPUT_VALIDATION_FAILED` (`FATAL`) when the
     *   transaction hash is missing or blank; or a re-thrown inner `KitError`
     *   from the attestation lookup, the re-attestation request, or the re-poll.
     *
     * @example
     * ```typescript
     * import { CCTPXBridgingProvider } from '@circle-fin/provider-cctpx'
     * import { Chains } from '@core/chains'
     *
     * const provider = new CCTPXBridgingProvider()
     *
     * const refreshed = await provider.reAttest(
     *   { adapter, address: '0xsource', chain: Chains.EthereumSepolia },
     *   '0xabc...',
     *   { maxRetries: 5 },
     * )
